  "travelerShortDescription": "A 3D SOCIAL TRAVEL EXPERIENCE COMBINING REAL-WORLD MOVEMENT WITH INTERACTIVE MAP EXPLORATION.",

  "travelerCatchPhrase": "WHERE GAMING MEETS SOCIAL MEDIA",
  
  "travelerLongDescription": "TRAVELER WAS DEVELOPED AS A RESPONSE TO THE GROWING DISCONNECT BETWEEN DIGITAL AND PHYSICAL EXPERIENCES. THE GOAL WAS TO CREATE AN APPLICATION THAT ENCOURAGES USERS TO EXPLORE THEIR REAL-WORLD ENVIRONMENT WHILE STILL ENJOYING INTERACTIVE DIGITAL FEATURES. THE APP COMBINES FLUTTER FOR A MODERN, INTUITIVE UI WITH UNITY FOR REAL-TIME 3D RENDERING. USING OPENSTREETMAP DATA, USERS CAN VISUALIZE THEIR SURROUNDINGS IN A DYNAMIC 3D ENVIRONMENT AND SEE BOTH THEIR OWN POSITION AND THAT OF THEIR FRIENDS. BY MERGING SOCIAL INTERACTION, GEOLOCATION, AND IMMERSIVE VISUALIZATION, TRAVELER TRANSFORMS MOVEMENT INTO A SHARED EXPERIENCE AND MOTIVATES USERS TO ACTIVELY EXPLORE THEIR ENVIRONMENT INSTEAD OF PASSIVELY CONSUMING CONTENT.",
  
  "travelerProjectReason": "THE MOTIVATION BEHIND TRAVELER WAS TO COUNTERBALANCE EXCESSIVE SCREEN TIME WITH MEANINGFUL REAL-WORLD INTERACTION. INSTEAD OF REPLACING REALITY, THE APP ENHANCES IT BY MAKING EXPLORATION ENGAGING, SOCIAL, AND VISUALLY IMMERSIVE. THE PROJECT ALSO SERVED AS AN OPPORTUNITY TO COMBINE MULTIPLE TECHNOLOGIES (FLUTTER + UNITY + GEOLOCATION SERVICES) INTO ONE COHESIVE PRODUCT AND TO EXPLORE HOW HYBRID SYSTEMS CAN DELIVER BOTH PERFORMANCE AND USABILITY.",

